WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.946
Assemble a forty to fifty minute lesson for your own grade band and subject.

2
00:00:05.146 --> 00:00:11.193
State the local content standard you already teach, the goal and two or three success criteria.

3
00:00:11.393 --> 00:00:17.174
Include a worked example, a partly supported attempt and a new independent response.

4
00:00:17.374 --> 00:00:20.757
Select a small toolchain that serves those stages.

5
00:00:20.957 --> 00:00:27.083
You do not need every app in the lesson; the course field guide remains available when another need appears.

6
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:29.808
Rehearse the lesson with an anonymous sample.

7
00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:32.849
Reopen the source and exported files.

8
00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:38.911
Check links, captions, reading order and a workable paper or low-tech alternative.

9
00:00:39.111 --> 00:00:43.702
If you include a game station, name its purpose and collect a debrief.

10
00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:50.344
Plan an individual response so that the evidence does not depend only on a group product or a game score.

11
00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:56.307
Use the capstone checklist to review the lesson and repair every criterion marked not yet.

12
00:00:56.507 --> 00:01:02.088
After teaching, compare initial and final explanations against the same criteria.

13
00:01:02.288 --> 00:01:06.824
Describe what changed in the reasoning and what you will change next time.

14
00:01:07.024 --> 00:01:11.635
Finish the course’s five knowledge checks and lesson steps in the LMS.

15
00:01:11.835 --> 00:01:18.991
The badge marks course completion; approved credit or external certification requires the provider’s separate

16
00:01:19.191 --> 00:01:20.448
authorization.
